hs retain their own licenses.","assistance":"AI-assisted architectural interpretation and procedural recipe authoring; deterministic Python/Blender export. No photographic textures.","review":{"status":"pending","reviewer":null,"checks":{}},"modelingNotes":["The principal polygon and 15 m total roof height come from OSM. Its untagged roof rise is interpreted as 4 m from the inspected front and oblique Commons images; the shallow polygonal roof uses an 18 m inset.","Two-storey rear annex and uncovered service footprint use an explicitly inferred 7 m eave/8 m roof. The central lantern radius 2.8 m and 17.2 m crown are visual estimates relative to the mapped auditorium; its height is not surveyed.","Upper window band, corner pilasters, strong cornices and a simplified ring of roundels retain the characteristic circus silhouette. The roundels suggest its sculpted frieze rather than reproduce the horses or lettering."],"source":{"url":"/objects/006c2b3379d3573273e3539c9df968f1dbb198ab9fd7101f6d105137ae5da9a9/source.blend.gz","bytes":157778,"sha256":"006c2b3379d3573273e3539c9df968f1dbb198ab9fd7101f6d105137ae5da9a9"},"spatialSource":{"url":"/objects/f6eb1c4cafa1d33940ad0a3185ed25fcb974fe09d27584838969ad53bca2508e/spatial-source.json","bytes":9044,"sha256":"f6eb1c4cafa1d33940ad0a3185ed25fcb974fe09d27584838969ad53bca2508e"},"preview":{"url":"/objects/be418ec05306064059476773f7b671efbca2d9b01bbf67864e7db851b531a165/preview.webp","bytes":5480,"sha256":"be418ec05306064059476773f7b671efbca2d9b01bbf67864e7db851b531a165"},"revision":"8fe32889622ef62855044f1aa7273434e51c0989142aad4ef5d332574d2b88cd","publicationRevision":"1f6a9027229be4de3e8a4888c9e97d704b213a2c462cc110f8f63cfbc072f179","bounds":[2.3671977,48.863145,2.3679858,48.8639277],"approved":false,"materialLibrary":{"schemaVersion":1,"sha256":"808c7d2073c712316c3ada02d6762b49c869f1e88399736045303c3739e4b7a4","url":"/materials/808c7d2073c712316c3ada02d6762b49c869f1e88399736045303c3739e4b7a4.json"},"metadata":"/assets/cirque-d